{
  "id": "p-technique-factor-analysis",
  "term": "P-technique factor analysis",
  "definition": "P-technique factor analysis is a form of factor analysis used on repeated measurements from one person over time to identify the latent factors that organize that individual’s pattern of covariation among variables. Unlike population-level R-technique analysis, it focuses on within-person structure and can reveal person-specific patterns or “signatures” that may differ from between-person results.",
